.TH Ludis 1 "2026" "ludis v0.9.3" "Ludis"
.SH NAME
ludis \- prefix manager for Wine/Proton runners and a Lutris game library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ludis
.RI [ command ] " [options] [arguments...]"
.br
.B ludis\-gui
[\fIfile.zgp\fR | \fIfile.zgr\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBludis\fR packages, installs, uninstalls and isolates Windows games running under Wine in Lutris, and manages Wine/Proton runners. Games and runners are exchanged as \fI.zgp\fR (game) and \fI.zgr\fR (runner) archives, produced and consumed locally.
.PP
\fBludis\fR is a terminal command that can be used in scripts: it never opens a window. Launched with no argument, it shows the help. The graphical interface is started with \fBludis\-gui\fR (also from the applications menu, or by double-clicking a \fI.zgp\fR or \fI.zgr\fR file).
.PP
This page is a summary. The complete documentation of every command (arguments, options, behavior, exit status, scripting notes, examples) is in the \fIdocs/commands/\fR folder of the project repository.
.SH COMMANDS \(em GAMES
.TP
.B install [\-y] [\-\-allow\-scripts] [\-\-replace] [\-\-ignore\-hash] <files.zgp...>
Installs games from .zgp archives. If a game is already installed, ludis asks to replace it (uninstall, then install; its saves are put aside and put back if a saves folder is set); \-\-replace answers yes in advance, without a terminal nothing is replaced.
.TP
.B uninstall [\-y] <slugs...>
Uninstalls games.
.TP
.B pack [\-LEVEL] [\-\-hash] <slugs...|\-\-all>
Packages games as .zgp archives.
.TP
.B isolate [\-y] <store|slug>
Splits a shared store prefix (Epic, EA, Ubisoft, Battle.net) into one prefix per game (beta).
.TP
.B list, list\-isolable
Lists installed games / games sharing a store prefix.
.TP
.B info <slug>
Shows the metadata of an installed game.
.TP
.B create\-prefix [\-y] <names...>
Creates empty Wine prefixes registered in Lutris.
.TP
.B exe\-install [\-y] <file>
Creates a prefix and runs a Windows installer in it.
.TP
.B shortcut <slugs...|\-\-all>
(Re)creates menu/desktop shortcuts.
.TP
.B icon, splash, logo <slugs...|\-\-all>
Fetches images from SteamGridDB (personal API key required).
.TP
.B sync\-media <slugs...|\-\-all>
Downloads Lutris's own media for games that lack them.
.TP
.B tools <slug> <tool> [args]
Runs a Wine tool on a game (winetricks, regedit, winecfg, console, exe, folder, favorite, env, runner, mangohud, overlay, gamepad).
.TP
.B saves dir [path] | <slug> status|backup|restore|export [file]|import <file>
Backs up, restores, exports (.zgs archive) and imports the saves of a game (AppData, Documents, Saved Games). The sync folder is set with "saves dir"; the previous local saves are always kept before a restore or an import.
.TP
.B vsync status | <slug> [status|on|off] [setting...]
Forces VSync off for a game with environment variables (d3d9, d3d11, d3d12, gl\-nvidia, gl\-mesa; none given = all).
.TP
.B lsfg <slugs...> on|off, lsfg status
Enables/disables lsfg-vk frame generation.
.TP
.B launcher <slugs...> on|off
Enables/disables the Ludis Launcher (loading screen and executable picker).
.TP
.B launcher\-entries <slug> get|set
Reads/replaces the launcher's picker entries (JSON).
.TP
.B killwine [\-y]
Kills every running Wine/Proton process.
.SH COMMANDS \(em RUNNERS
.TP
.B install\-runner [\-y] <files.zgr|names...>
Installs runners from local archives or the GitHub release.
.TP
.B uninstall\-runner [\-y] <names...>
Uninstalls runners.
.TP
.B pack\-runner [\-LEVEL] [\-\-hash] <names...|\-\-all>
Packages runners as .zgr archives.
.TP
.B list\-runner, list\-remote\-runners
Lists installed / remotely available runners.
.TP
.B game\-version <slug> [value|\-\-clear]
Shows, sets or removes the version number of a game (free text, 32 characters at most). It is written into the package at export and shown when another package of the game is installed over it.
.SH COMMANDS \(em SYSTEM
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnoses the machine (Lutris, runners, required and optional tools) and says what is missing. Changes nothing, downloads nothing; exit code 1 if something required is missing.
.TP
.B check
Checks that the runners needed by installed games are present and fetches missing ones.
.TP
.B lutris\-defaults [status|runner [name]|winetricks [system|runner]]
Shows/sets the default Wine runner and which winetricks (system or the one bundled with the runner) Lutris uses by default. A game with its own value keeps it.
.TP
.B lutris\-version [flatpak|native|reset]
Shows/forces the Lutris installation used when both exist.
.TP
.B self\-update [check|install]
Checks for a newer ludis release and installs it (package installs only).
.TP
.B log [\-n N|\-\-all|\-\-grep PATTERN|\-\-clear]
Shows, filters or clears the action log.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-y
Automatically answers yes to the command's general confirmation question (it does not skip the hash and embedded-script questions).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-scripts
install: accepts embedded launch/close scripts of a .zgp without asking (only for packages you trust).
.TP
.B \-\-ignore\-hash
install, install\-runner: skips the sha256 sidecar check.
.TP
.B \-\-hash
pack, pack\-runner: writes a sha256 sidecar file next to each archive.
.TP
.B \-0 \&... \-22
pack, pack\-runner: zstd compression level.
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-v
Shows the ludis version.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h
Shows this page (or a built-in summary if it is not installed).
.PP
Global options must be placed right after the command name, before its other arguments (for example \fBludis install \-y game.zgp\fR).
.SH LOG
Errors printed by commands, and some successes, are recorded in \fI~/.local/share/ludis/ludis.log\fR (always under the home directory), one line per event with four tab-separated columns: timestamp, origin, status (OK, ERROR, WARN or INFO), detail. Past 10000 lines the file is renamed \fIludis.log.1\fR and a fresh log is started. See \fBlog\fR above.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ludis/ludis.log
Action log.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ludis/
ludis configuration (SteamGridDB key, Lutris version choice, lsfg\-vk).
.TP
.I <game_dir>/ludis\-launcher.yml
Launcher picker entries.
.TP
.I ~/.config/lutris/ (native package) / ~/.var/app/net.lutris.Lutris/ (Flatpak)
Lutris configuration and database, read and modified by ludis.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project repository (https://github.com/RogerBytes/ludis), folder \fIdocs/commands/\fR: one page per command, the global options (\fIoptions.md\fR) and the archive formats (\fIarchives.md\fR).
.SH AUTHOR
Ludis (ludis) is a personal project.
